What:		/sys/bus/usb/devices/<INTERFACE>/billboard/num_modes
Date:		November 2026
Contact:	linux-usb@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Number of Alternate Modes listed by the USB Billboard device
		(bNumberOfAlternateModes).

What:		/sys/bus/usb/devices/<INTERFACE>/billboard/preferred_mode
Date:		November 2026
Contact:	linux-usb@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Index of the Alternate Mode the device prefers
		(bPreferredAlternateMode).

What:		/sys/bus/usb/devices/<INTERFACE>/billboard/vconn_power
Date:		November 2026
Contact:	linux-usb@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		VCONN power the device needs to run all its Alternate Modes:
		"1W", "1.5W", "2W", "3W", "4W", "5W", "6W", "not-required" or
		"reserved".

What:		/sys/bus/usb/devices/<INTERFACE>/billboard/version
Date:		November 2026
Contact:	linux-usb@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Billboard specification version the device implements
		(bcdVersion), e.g. "1.21".

What:		/sys/bus/usb/devices/<INTERFACE>/billboard/additional_failure_info
Date:		November 2026
Contact:	linux-usb@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		bAdditionalFailureInfo as reported by the device, in hex.

What:		/sys/bus/usb/devices/<INTERFACE>/billboard/additional_info_url
Date:		November 2026
Contact:	linux-usb@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		The device's iAddtionalInfoURL string, empty if it has none.

What:		/sys/bus/usb/devices/<INTERFACE>/billboard/altmode<N>_svid
What:		/sys/bus/usb/devices/<INTERFACE>/billboard/altmode<N>_mode
What:		/sys/bus/usb/devices/<INTERFACE>/billboard/altmode<N>_vdo
What:		/sys/bus/usb/devices/<INTERFACE>/billboard/altmode<N>_description
Date:		November 2026
Contact:	linux-usb@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Alternate Mode <N> as listed by the device: the Standard or
		Vendor ID in hex (wSVID), the mode index within that SVID
		(bAlternateMode), the mode's VDO from the Billboard AUM
		Capability descriptor (only present when the device provides
		one) and the iAlternateModeString string (empty if none).

What:		/sys/bus/usb/devices/<INTERFACE>/billboard/altmode<N>_state
Date:		November 2026
Contact:	linux-usb@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Result of the host's attempt to enter Alternate Mode <N>, from
		bmConfigured: "configured", "not-attempted" (not attempted or
		exited), "failed" (attempted but not entered) or "error"
		(unspecified error). The driver also logs a warning for each
		"failed" or "error" mode when it binds.
